---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import MermaidDiagram from '../components/MermaidDiagram.astro';
import { templatesDiagram } from '../data/diagrams';
---

<DocsLayout title="Templates" sectionLabel="How It Works" activeSlug="templates">

  <div class="panel-intro">
    <h2>Templates</h2>
    <p>Templates are the <strong>scaffolding blueprints</strong> VibeCrew uses to create consistent, well-structured artifacts across every project. From the initial VISION.md to test configs and session logs, every file that VibeCrew generates starts from a template. This ensures consistency, reduces agent token cost (no need to invent formats from scratch), and makes outputs predictable.</p>
    <div class="key-points">
      <div class="key-point">
        <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
        <div>
          <strong>What they are</strong>
          <p>Template files in the <code>templates/</code> directory: Markdown documents, JSON schemas, test configs, CI/CD pipelines, and a full VitePress documentation site scaffold. Agents fill in project-specific content while the structure stays consistent.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="key-point">
        <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
        <div>
          <strong>What problem they solve</strong>
          <p>Without templates, agents would invent different file formats each session &mdash; inconsistent backlog schemas, varying session log structures, and unpredictable CLAUDE.md layouts. Templates guarantee that every artifact works with every script, hook, and dashboard component.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Tier 1 Foundation ── -->
  <section class="section">
    <h3>Tier 1 Foundation Templates</h3>
    <p>These templates drive the <code>/new-project</code> workflow. Each foundation step produces a file from its template, filled with project-specific content by the responsible agent.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Template</th><th>Output</th><th>Created By</th><th>What It Defines</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>VISION.md.template</code></td>
            <td><code>VISION.md</code></td>
            <td>Orchestrator</td>
            <td>Product vision, target audience, core value proposition, success metrics, and project scope.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>design-system.css.template</code></td>
            <td><code>design-system.css</code></td>
            <td>Design Discovery or Import</td>
            <td>CSS custom properties: colors, typography, spacing, radius, shadows, breakpoints &mdash; the design token file.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>design-brief.md.template</code></td>
            <td><code>design-brief.md</code></td>
            <td>Design Discovery or Import</td>
            <td>Rationale for design decisions &mdash; why these colors, fonts, and styles. Agents reference this during feature development.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>tdr.md.template</code></td>
            <td><code>TDR.md</code></td>
            <td>Stack Scout</td>
            <td>Technology Decision Record: framework, database, auth, hosting, testing, CI, with Token Impact Assessment for each choice.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>roadmap.md.template</code></td>
            <td><code>ROADMAP.md</code></td>
            <td>Orchestrator</td>
            <td>Feature roadmap with priority phases, dependencies, and estimated complexity.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>CLAUDE.md.template</code></td>
            <td><code>CLAUDE.md</code></td>
            <td>Orchestrator</td>
            <td>Project-level AI rules: conventions, constraints, architecture patterns, and session learnings. Kept under 200 lines.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── State & Config ── -->
  <section class="section">
    <h3>State &amp; Config Templates</h3>
    <p>Created during <code>/setup</code> to initialize the <code>.vibecrew/</code> runtime directory. These define the JSON schemas that scripts, hooks, and the dashboard all rely on.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Template</th><th>Output</th><th>What It Defines</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>config.json.template</code></td>
            <td><code>.vibecrew/config.json</code></td>
            <td>Terminal preference, notifications, user profile dimensions, cost thresholds, MCP server toggles.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>state.json.template</code></td>
            <td><code>.vibecrew/state.json</code></td>
            <td>Foundation completion flags, active feature, current phase, feature history.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>backlog.json.template</code></td>
            <td><code>.vibecrew/backlog.json</code></td>
            <td>Feature specs with Kanban columns, priority, complexity, acceptance criteria, and dependencies.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>gamification.json.template</code></td>
            <td><code>.vibecrew/gamification.json</code></td>
            <td>XP, level, badge definitions, skill tree, streak tracking, challenge completions.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── Testing & Quality ── -->
  <section class="section">
    <h3>Testing &amp; Quality Templates</h3>
    <p>Scaffolded into the project when the corresponding testing command is first used. Each template follows best practices for its test framework.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Template</th><th>Output</th><th>What It Configures</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>vitest.config.ts.template</code></td>
            <td><code>vitest.config.ts</code></td>
            <td>Unit testing with Vitest: coverage thresholds, test environment, setup files.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>playwright.config.ts.template</code></td>
            <td><code>playwright.config.ts</code></td>
            <td>E2E testing with Playwright: browsers, base URL, screenshot/video settings.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>axe-config.ts.template</code></td>
            <td><code>axe.config.ts</code></td>
            <td>Accessibility testing with axe-core: WCAG 2.1 AA rules, element selectors.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>k6-config.js.template</code></td>
            <td><code>k6.config.js</code></td>
            <td>Performance testing with k6: load, stress, spike, and soak test scenarios.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>test-utils.ts.template</code></td>
            <td><code>test-utils.ts</code></td>
            <td>Shared test utilities: render helpers, mock factories, custom matchers.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── Reporting ── -->
  <section class="section">
    <h3>Reporting Templates</h3>
    <p>Structured JSON schemas for every type of report VibeCrew generates. These ensure consistent machine-readable output that the dashboard and scripts can parse.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Template</th><th>Generated By</th><th>What It Captures</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>session-log.json.template</code></td><td><code>/wrap</code></td><td>Session timestamps, features worked on, Vibe Score, token usage, estimated cost.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>score-breakdown.json.template</code></td><td><code>/wrap</code></td><td>Detailed Vibe Score: each deduction and bonus with reasons and line items.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>handoff.md.template</code></td><td><code>/handoff</code></td><td>Structured context transfer: current state, pending work, blockers, next steps.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>audit-report.json.template</code></td><td><code>/audit</code></td><td>OWASP findings: vulnerability type, severity, file location, remediation.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>ci-heal-report.json.template</code></td><td><code>/heal</code></td><td>CI failure diagnosis: category, each fix attempt, outcome.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>simplification-report.json.template</code></td><td><code>/simplify</code></td><td>Dead code, over-abstractions, API surface bloat with before/after diffs.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>mutation-proposal.json.template</code></td><td>Performance Coach</td><td>CLAUDE.md rule proposals: anti-pattern detected, proposed rule, evidence.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── CI/CD & Docs ── -->
  <section class="section">
    <h3>CI/CD &amp; Documentation Templates</h3>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Template</th><th>What It Creates</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>github-actions-autofix.yml.template</code></td><td>GitHub Actions workflow for automated issue fixing &mdash; triggers on <code>issues.labeled</code> events.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>gitlab-ci-autofix.yml.template</code></td><td>GitLab CI pipeline for automated issue fixing &mdash; pipeline-triggered equivalent.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>feature-spec.md.template</code></td><td>Feature specification format: problem statement, acceptance criteria, dependencies, complexity.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>CONTRIBUTING.md.template</code></td><td>Contributing guidelines for the project.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>gitignore-additions.template</code></td><td>Git ignore entries for <code>.vibecrew/</code> runtime files that shouldn't be committed.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>docs-site/</code></td><td>Full VitePress documentation site scaffold with 7-tab dashboard, data loaders, and Vue components.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── Reference Data ── -->
  <section class="section">
    <h3>Reference Data</h3>
    <p>Static data files that agents and scripts reference but don't modify per-project.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>What It Contains</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>mcp-registry.json</code></td><td>25 MCP server definitions with trigger patterns, commands, env vars, and docs links. Powers TDR-based auto-discovery.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>badge-catalog.json</code></td><td>Achievement badge definitions: names, unlock conditions, XP rewards, icons.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>challenge-pool.json</code></td><td>Gamification challenges: daily, weekly, and milestone challenges with reward criteria.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>signal-schema.json</code></td><td>Inter-agent signal file validation schema. Hooks validate signals against this before writes.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>architecture-diagrams/</code></td><td>5 Mermaid diagram templates (<code>.mmd</code>) for system topology, ER schema, state flows, API sequences, and component tree.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <MermaidDiagram chart={templatesDiagram} caption="Template categories and when they're used in the VibeCrew lifecycle" />

</DocsLayout>
